      "message": "Hi John,\n\nThanks for posting this.  One question though: do we know if this will work for all types of tasks in the kernel? heap-\u003eops-\u003eallocate() is expected to return an fd generated by dma_buf_fd(). dma_buf_fd() calls fd_install() (https://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/latest/source/fs/file.c#L616), and I don\u0027t know whether this function works universally for all  types tasks.  For  for instance, will this work for kthreads or workqueues?\n\nThanks,\n\nChris.",
      "revId": "7db57ffe811426852ef37bed0e68e749e9a45140",
